    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d377">

                <pb facs="0430" n="346" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg346"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. No. 763.72113/639</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morgan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-02T15:00:00-03:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 2, 1918, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received August 3, 8.53 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Minister of Finance confirmed to me today current report that Brazilian
                    Government is taking over and liquidating the three German banks as well as the
                    principal German houses in Brazil with capital and offices in Germany. Please
                    telegraph <hi rendition="#italic">résumé</hi> of manner in which German houses
                    in the United States are treated whose capital and offices are wholly located in
                    the United States.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
